  "document": "Manon Lescaut (Auber)\nManon Lescaut is an opera or opéra comique in 3 acts by Daniel Auber to a libretto by Eugène Scribe, and, like Puccini's \"Manon Lescaut\" and Massenet's \"Manon\", is based on the Abbé Prévost's novel \"Manon Lescaut\". Auber's version is nowadays the least-performed of the three."
